  "title": "Kinkaku-ji (Golden Pavilion), Kyoto",
  "summary": "Kinkaku-ji's Relics Hall, known as the Golden Pavilion, stands in Kyoto on ground where the shogun Ashikaga Yoshimitsu began building his Kitayama residence in 1397. The original pavilion was burned down in 1950 and rebuilt in 1955, and the temple was designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1994.",
